nodecode-flashdata is a rewrite of rocosen's rocosen/flashdata-mcp:
https://github.com/rocosen/flashdata-mcp, commit 23e0d9849b2546767741fabfc454fb0089f1cb58,
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 FlashData contributors (LICENSE).

What was rewritten: the plugin was declarative - an mcp.json naming the hosted
FlashData MCP endpoint with the key in an X-API-Key header, a plugin.json
declaring one secret setting, and fifteen Skills over the server's tools. This
cell speaks the same JSON-RPC to the same endpoint itself: the handshake, the
tool call, the JSON and event-stream answers, and the fifteen operations
(Google web, news, image, shopping, video and places search; YouTube search,
extended search, metadata, transcript, captions, trainability, channel,
suggestions and storage delivery; and the pricing, job and result reads) as
their own verbs, with three model tools in front of them. The renderer is new:
the original left the reading of each answer to the Skill, this one numbers a
result list and clips a long answer to the section's bounds.

What was left out: the fifteen Skills as separate prose documents (their
argument names and limits are now the primer and the tool schemas), the
Hermes approval and secret plumbing (Nodecode owns both), and youtube_download
as a verb of its own - it takes a storage object with the operator's own
credentials, so it is reached through flashdata:call rather than a signature
this cell would have to guess.
